diff --git a/docs/JOT-INTEGRATION.md b/docs/JOT-INTEGRATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..4216fd33
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/JOT-INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Optional Jot feature
+
+This contribution adds Jot to the existing Features hub, Sound group, settings navigation/search, menu panel and Dynamic Island Controls. It is opt-in, follows the normal install/uninstall behavior, and preserves saved choices. It does not change Vorssaint branding, bundle IDs, signing, fans, or updater behavior.
+
+Jot is a separate optional app. Installing or opening this feature never starts speech capture. Open Jot launches the app explicitly. Play/Pause and Start/End Meeting use Jot's local API; Quit Jot sends Jot a normal macOS Quit request, keeping Vorssaint open. When Jot is missing or disconnected the controller shows a connection message and disables capture actions. Install Jot separately before using it.
+
+The bridge reads only the text-free `speech.controls` snapshot over Jot's same-user Unix socket at `~/Library/Application Support/Jot/service.sock`. It validates the socket peer UID, bounds requests and responses, and permits only fixed control methods. It requests no microphone, transcription, history, or insertion permission. It never reads transcript endpoints. `space.jot.app.controlsChanged` notifications are payload-free invalidation hints. An idle two-second refresh recovers missed hints; fast level refresh happens only during a Fn action. Disabling/uninstalling stops the timer and observer and dismisses its notice. Jot remains the capture/history/insertion owner.
+
+Hold-Fn activity shows capture level, processing, and the actual insertion/review outcome. Double-Fn keeps Jot's field-anchored preview and explicit Tab acceptance. Reconnection establishes a fresh baseline rather than replaying a completion. Reduce Motion uses a static mark.
+
+Jot's standalone menu bar is on by default and the app remains independently usable. Consolidating icons is optional; the current personal Jot setting recognizes the temporary custom controller identity, so a stock Vorssaint installation never inadvertently hides Jot merely by being open.
+
+## Validation and remaining work
+
+Build with `./build.sh --dev`. Run `./build.sh --test-suite=features`, `--test-suite=settings` and `--test-suite=notch`. Feature tests cover opt-in defaults, install/uninstall, settings and shortcut visibility, permission ownership, and saved off choices.
+
+Before upstream merge, review the contribution with the maintainer, translate the new English copy, and exercise the settings/Features screens plus physical Fn/Tab insertion and meeting controls on a Mac with Jot installed. Jot's public signing/notarization and distribution readiness are a separate release gate. This is a prepared contribution, not an accepted upstream release or a new plugin system.
